# The scenario editor (EDIT.BAS), written by hand. It leaves Starting Year once with Esc. It
# then loads 1939, changes a technology level,
# the cash, a city's fort, the navy and the side, saves the scenario as 1939 again, loads it
# back, and quits. The run's saved files are checked by their hashes (the "#! files" line):
# the scenario and map as saved, and the backups that SHELL "copy" made of the originals.
#! program edit
#! files scenarios/WW1939.INI scenarios/EURO1939.DAT scenarios/WW1939.BAK scenarios/EURO1939.BAK

# Starting Year: Esc, which brings the same menu back (getyr's exit by RETURN), then the first
# entry, EURO1939.DAT.
play until 2:S
digest
key esc
play until 2:S
digest
key enter

# Technology: the second entry, one level up.
play until 2:M
digest
text t
play until 2:A
digest
key down
prompt
key enter
play until 7
digest
key up
play until 7
key enter

# Cash, the entry below Technology: doubled.
play until 2:M
digest
key down
prompt
key enter
play until 7
key pageup
play until 7
digest
key enter

# Fortify: the first city whose name starts with B, then one level up.
play until 2:M
text f
play until 2:C
text b
play until 2:C
digest
key enter
play until 7
key up
play until 7
digest
key enter

# Navy, Edit: one ship more.
play until 2:M
digest
text n
play until 2:N
text e
play until 7
key up
play until 7
digest
key enter

# Side: now the Axis side, then back to the Allied side.
play until 2:M
text s
play until 2:M
digest
text s

# Save, the fourth entry from the end: as 1939, its month as it is, its description as it is.
play until 2:M
key pagedown
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
digest
key enter
play until 2:S
digest
key enter
play until 2:B
digest
key enter
play until 4
key enter

# Load: 1939 again, now the edited scenario.
play until 2:M
digest
text l
play until 2:S
key enter
play until 2:M
digest

# Quit, then Yes by its letter, and a key for END's "Press any key to continue".
text q
play until 2:L
digest
text y
repeat space
